                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.05870/2610.05870v1/index_vector.png",
                "caption": "Fig. 3:Computing of the Authenticity Score.Given an input imagexx, a reconstruction-free inverterGe−1G_{e}^{-1}produces an inverted reconstructionx~\\tilde{x}. We then compute complementary similarities betweenxxandx~\\tilde{x}: pixel fidelity(PSNR), structural fidelity(SSIM), perceptual distance(1−1{-}LPIPS), and semantic consistency (CLIPcosine). A calibrated weighted combiner (learnedα1,α2,α3,α4\\alpha_{1},\\alpha_{2},\\alpha_{3},\\alpha_{4}) produces a scalarss(xx,x~\\tilde{x}), yielding the A-index in[0,1][0,1]. A safety thresholdτ\\taucertifies content asAuthenticwhenA-index≥τ\\text{A-index}\\geq\\tau, and otherwise labels it asPlausibly Deniable. We further analyze robustness by applyingℓ∞\\ell_{\\infty}-bounded perturbationsδ\\delta(PGD-style) throughGe−1G_{e}^{-1}to maximize or minimize the A-index.",
                "position": 511
            }
        ]
